    <GaugingStation location="Millbrook" name="Grwyne" number="56012">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump weir of reinforced concrete and local stone with phosphor bronze crest. Reservoirs in catchment affect runoff.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Limited u/s shoaling and weed growth on weir may affect low flows. Fish counter on d/s side of weir not thought to affect performance. Flows contained up to 2.27m. No bypassing on either bank at high flows - channel contained by road wall on lb. Three peak flow ratings applied across period of record. NRW confirm no high flow gaugings; highest gauging at 7.6 cumecs. Reservoirs in catchment affect runoff.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Crump weir of reinforced concrete and local stone with phosphor bronze crest, 10.67m wide.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Gap in data between 1985 and 1988. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Impermeable, predominantly Old Red Sandstone conglomerates, sandstone and marl. Predominantly grassland for livestock farming, significant heathland and some afforestation.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">S</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, rating has been extended using a hydraulic model." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating cannot be validated beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
